    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d436">

                <pb facs="0405" n="289" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg289"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 322.112G64/3.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister of Ecuador to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translations.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of Ecuador</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-12-11">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 11, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: The last mail from Ecuador
                    brought me instructions from my Government to confer with your excellency over a
                    petition filed by Goo Kwai, a Chinaman naturalized in the United States, who
                    wishes to repair to Ecuador on a visit to his family.</p>
                <p>For that purpose and with your excellency’s kind note No. 11 of the 7th instant
                    before me, I have the honor to assure you that I shall be glad to talk over the
                    matter with you when I next call at the Department, of which I will let your
                    excellency know the evening before.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">G. S. Córdova</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
